# A Porsche 911 GT3 R of the 992 generation: the numbers its behaviour follows from.
#
# From Porsche Motorsport's published data: a 4,194 cc flat six behind the rear axle making up
# to 416 kW (565 PS), a six-speed sequential gearbox, a wheelbase of 2,507 mm, 2,039 mm wide at
# the front axle and 2,050 mm at the rear, and 1,250 kg before the driver and fuel. What Porsche
# doesn't publish (spring rates, the torque curve's shape, downforce) is set to what the class
# runs, and checked by driving it: crates/solstice-vehicle/tests/gt3r.rs.

mass 1330                          # with its driver and fuel
inertia 1650 1800 520              # pitch, yaw, roll
centre 0 0.4 0.226                 # 59% of its weight on the rear axle
body 1.96 0.95 4.55 at 0 0.67 0

front at=1.2535 track=1.70 radius=0.34 inertia=1.5 driven=no
front spring=110000 bump=6800 rebound=10000 bar=38000 travel=0.065,0.075 roll_centre=0.03
front brake=3100 grip=1
rear at=1.2535 track=1.72 radius=0.355 inertia=2.0 driven=yes
rear spring=179000 bump=10400 rebound=14500 bar=16000 travel=0.07,0.08 roll_centre=0.08
rear brake=2500 grip=1.07          # the rear tyres are wider, and carry more

engine idle=1100 limit=9250 inertia=0.11 friction=30,0.01
torque 1500 290
torque 2000 330
torque 3000 390
torque 4000 440
torque 5000 480
torque 6000 500
torque 6500 505
torque 7000 500
torque 7500 492
torque 8000 482
torque 8400 473                    # 416 kW here
torque 8800 448
torque 9250 415
torque 9600 360

gears 3.34 2.5 1.95 1.58 1.31 1.113
final 3.9
reverse 3
gearbox shift=0.05 efficiency=0.93 clutch=900
diff preload=80 power=0.5 coast=0.35

aero drag=0.95 downforce=2.1 balance=0.36
steering lock=26 ackermann=0.6
geometry anti_dive=0.25 anti_squat=0.35
assists abs=yes traction=yes stability=yes
